  "title": "Higher-order awareness is thought, not inner sense",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "06935cc7-dcdb-4f20-b7be-8b35c6cc8921",
      "text": "Sensing always involves mental qualities, but the higher-order awareness of conscious states has no mental qualities of its own, only those of the states it is about. So that awareness is not a higher-order perception, as inner sense theories hold, but a higher-order thought.",
